 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**Yes, but more slowly than in 2023.** Eating out in Melbourne rose 3.5% in the year to August 2026, according to the ABS Consumer Price Index (the \"meals out and take-away foods\" group).\n\n- **Latest (Aug 2026):** up 3.5% on a year earlier. The national figure was 4.1%, so Melbourne is running a little below the average.\n- **Recent trend:** the annual rate has climbed back up after a soft patch. It was 2.3% in the June 2025 quarter, then rose to 3.5–3.9% from late 2025. It peaked at 4.4% in May 2026 and was 4.1% in July.\n- **Earlier:** price rises were much steeper in 2023. Melbourne meals out were up 7.0% in the March 2023 quarter and 5.8% in the March 2024 quarter, before slowing.\n\nIn index terms, the Melbourne series reached 103.29 in August 2026, against 100 in September 2025.",
